  "Question": "A positive number \\(x\\) has the property that \\(x\\%\\) of \\(x\\) is \\(4.\\) What is \\(x?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(20\\)",
    "E": "\\(40\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A percent means out of \\(100\\), so \\(x\\%\\) of \\(x\\) is \\(\\frac{x}{100}\\cdot x\\). The given condition therefore becomes\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{100}=4,\n\\]\nwhich gives \\(x^2=400\\). The two real square roots of \\(400\\) are \\(20\\) and \\(-20\\). Since \\(x\\) is positive, \\(x=\\boxed{20}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
